    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569-a4">

                <pb facs="0801" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg695"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Le Messurier to Captain Evans.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Newfoundland Customs,<lb/>Assistant Collector’s
                                Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port of St.
                            Johns</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-02-02"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">2d February,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to notify you that one
                    seine and five dories landed by you, out of the American fishing schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Edna Wallace Hopper</hi>, at Jennings Cove, Middle Arm,
                    Bay of Islands, have been seized by this department for a violation of the
                    customs act; and this is to duly notify you of the same and to inform you that
                    your schooner and person are also liable to the penalties provided under the
                    act.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Le
                            Messurier</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy Minister of
                            Customs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
